bio:
Born Sheffield 
 
Upperthorpe Comrades, Gainsborough Trinity then Rotherham County (sept 1922), Jack Lambert joined Rotherham in April 1923 and on 12.5.23 both he and Bernie were in Rotherham side that beat Barnsley 2-1 at Hillsborough to win Sheffield County Cup 
 
Sheffield United (July 1923), 
 
Luton Town (July 1928); 
 
QPR (July 1929 to end of 31/32) - debut in Div 3 (South) 31.8.29 Crystal Palace 1 QPR 1 
 
Llanelli (July 1932); 
 
PROBABLY Merthyr and then to Swindon Town (July 1933); 
 
Margate (July 1934) ex Merthyr when played for us  - 23.2.35 played whole game in goal as Margate beat Southend 6-1 in friendly at Hartsdown
 
With Ramsgate 35/36 and sent off in 4-1 defeat at Sittingbourne on 11.1.36 - left them when they went out of business end of that season
 
Widely quoted dob's of 14.3.01 or 14.3.99 are incorrect

5' 9" born Hackney- 
Career: Peel Institute; Clapton Orient (amateur) Mar. 1906 (league debut v. Gainsborough Trinity 24.3.06. Made 7 League and Cup appearance for Orient, 1 goal. 
Left Orient early in 1906/07 season; Leyton (early 1906/07) - 7 appearances, l goal; 
Tufnell Park 1908-10 - represented Middlesex against Norfolk in 1908, and won a Southern Counties Amateur Championship medal. 
Briefly at Doncaster 1910 
then to Sheff U Sheffield United July 1910 (9 League appearances, 2 goals); 
Halifax Town Aug. 1912; 
Merthyr Town 1912/13; 
Brentford Aug. 1913; 
Fulham Apr. 1914 (9 League appearances, 4 goals); joined at same time as future MFC player Cannon
Fulham to QPR (Southern League) as amateur Nov. 1914. QPR debut 14.11.14 QPR 0 Exeter 2 in SL. 7 gls in 19 apps 14/15  // 17 apps 5 gls 15/16 (London Combination) //  16/17 1 app 0 goal in Dec 1916 London Comb.  // 17/18 and 18/19 no apps but on books 
also guested for Tottenham Hotspur and Norwich City during war years; 
Margate (in from QPR) 19/20 - - Margate 20/21 -  
Norwich City Sept. 1920 (3 League appearances, no goals); 
Merthyr Town again 
Joined Charlton Athletic 20.6.21 (no first team appearances) left club Apr. 1924 Charlton 21/22 - their first Football League season.  Kosha Goodman there too.  Didn't make any appearances though.        
Tommy's father was a former groundsman at Clapton Orient died Stoke Newington, London, 26.8.56 aged 68   
 Full name Henry Thomas Simons
